---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Join the Order
permalink: /join/
description: "Create an EGregoRA account or sign in — a verified email address, and then your face or fingerprint. No passwords, anywhere."
---

<section class="page-head">
  <p class="kicker">The Threshold</p>
  <h1>Join the Order</h1>
  <p class="lede muted">No passwords. An address you can prove is yours, and after that your own face or
  fingerprint if your device has one. Membership costs nothing, confers no rank, and withholds no teaching —
  everything on this site stays public. An account simply means the oracle knows who it is talking to.</p>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal" id="gate">
  <div class="frame frame--first illuminated">
    <div class="auth-box" id="auth-box" data-state="start">

      <!-- ------------------------------------------------ signed out --- -->
      <div class="auth-pane" data-pane="start">
        <p class="kicker">STEP ONE · YOUR ADDRESS</p>
        <h2>Sign in, or create an account</h2>
        <p class="muted small">One form does both. If the address is new, an account is made; if it is known,
        you are signed back in. Either way a six-digit code goes to the inbox and nothing is created until
        you enter it.</p>

        <div class="social-door" id="social-door" hidden>
          <p class="muted xsmall">Or come in with an account you already have. It signs you in if we
          know the address and makes the account if we do not. We take the address and the name, and
          nothing else; no password is ever seen here. Proving a Google account is not proof of age,
          so the studio check below is still asked for separately.</p>
          <div class="social-row" id="social-row"></div>
          <p class="auth-msg xsmall" id="social-msg"></p>
        </div>

        <p class="muted xsmall"><strong style="color:inherit">One account, both sites.</strong> The same
        address signs you in at <a href="https://the-two-infinities.hatchable.site/">The Two Infinities
        (and beyond)</a> &mdash; the sister site, turned to astronomy and the galactic torus. Join at
        either and the other already knows you, age check included. There is one mailing list between
        them, and one click leaves it.</p>

        <form class="ornate" id="auth-start-form">
          <div>
            <label for="a-email">Email address</label>
            <input id="a-email" type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email"
                   inputmode="email" placeholder="rowan@example.org">
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="a-name">Name <span class="muted xsmall">(optional — what the oracle should call you)</span></label>
            <input id="a-name" type="text" name="name" maxlength="80" autocomplete="name"
                   placeholder="Rowan of the North">
          </div>
          <div class="captcha" data-captcha="join">
            <p class="captcha-label">Read the gate-word and type it back</p>
            <div class="captcha-row">
              <div class="captcha-art" data-captcha-art aria-live="polite"></div>
              <button class="captcha-new" type="button" data-captcha-new
                      title="Draw another word" aria-label="Draw another gate-word">&#8634;</button>
            </div>
            <input type="text" data-captcha-input autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="characters"
                   spellcheck="false" maxlength="8" required
                   aria-label="The gate-word" placeholder="The five letters above">
          </div>
          <div class="ask-actions">
            <button class="btn" type="submit" id="a-send">Send my code</button>
            <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="a-bio" hidden>
              <span aria-hidden="true">☉</span> Use face or fingerprint
            </button>
          </div>
        </form>
        <p class="auth-msg" id="a-msg" role="status"></p>
        <p class="muted xsmall">Confirming your address also puts you on the order's mailing list —
        new pages from both sites, the podcast, and the occasional long letter from Ed. Not weekly, never sold, and the
        way off it sits at the foot of every one of them, one click, no reason asked.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- -------------------------------------------------- the code --- -->
      <div class="auth-pane" data-pane="code" hidden>
        <p class="kicker">STEP TWO · THE SIX DIGITS</p>
        <h2>Check your inbox</h2>
        <p class="muted small" id="a-code-note">A code is on its way. It lasts fifteen minutes and works once.</p>
        <form class="ornate" id="auth-code-form">
          <div>
            <label for="a-code">Verification code</label>
            <input id="a-code" type="text" name="code" required inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*"
                   maxlength="6" autocomplete="one-time-code" class="code-input" placeholder="000000">
          </div>
          <div class="ask-actions">
            <button class="btn" type="submit" id="a-check">Verify and enter</button>
            <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="a-again">Send another</button>
            <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="a-back">Different address</button>
          </div>
        </form>
        <p class="auth-msg" id="a-code-msg" role="status"></p>
      </div>

      <!-- --------------------------------------------------- signed in -- -->
      <div class="auth-pane" data-pane="in" hidden>
        <p class="kicker">INSIDE</p>
        <h2 id="a-greeting">Welcome</h2>
        <p class="muted small" id="a-who"></p>

        <div class="auth-id" id="a-id-block">
          <h3>Age &amp; identity — the studio door</h3>
          <p class="muted small" id="a-id-state">The image and video generators are the one part of this
          site kept behind a check. Everything else is open to everyone, signed in or not. There are two
          ways through: a look at your face, which takes seconds, or a document, which always works.</p>

          <div class="scan-box" id="scan-box">
            <p class="kicker">THE QUICK WAY · A LOOK AT YOUR FACE</p>
            <p class="muted small">Let the camera see you for a moment and a published face model
            estimates your age. <strong>The estimate is computed inside this page</strong> — the model is
            fetched once and run in your browser, so the frames are read where they are taken. Seven
            readings are averaged, the median is used, and no face print, template or biometric of any
            kind is kept. If the reading lands anywhere near eighteen the studio asks for a document
            instead: estimation is only good to a few years, so the line is drawn at twenty-five.</p>
            <p class="muted xsmall">The first scan downloads about a megabyte of model weights, so give it
            a moment. If your browser blocks the download, or the camera, the document check below always
            works.</p>

            <div class="scan-stage" id="scan-stage">
              <video id="scan-video" playsinline muted hidden></video>
              <div class="scan-ring" id="scan-ring" hidden aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <p class="scan-hint" id="scan-hint">Face a window if you can. Fill the oval with your head,
              take off sunglasses, and look straight at the lens.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="ask-actions">
              <button class="btn" type="button" id="scan-start">Scan my face</button>
              <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="scan-shoot" hidden>Take the reading</button>
              <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="scan-stop" hidden>Stop the camera</button>
            </div>
            <p class="auth-msg" id="scan-msg" role="status"></p>
            <p class="muted xsmall" id="scan-unsupported" hidden>This browser will not give a page camera
            access, so the document check below is your way through.</p>
          </div>

          <p class="scan-or"><span>or show a document</span></p>

          <form class="ornate" id="id-form">
            <div>
              <label for="i-legal">Full legal name, as printed on the document</label>
              <input id="i-legal" name="legal_name" type="text" required maxlength="140"
                     autocomplete="name" placeholder="Rowan Alexander Gregory">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="i-dob">Date of birth</label>
              <input id="i-dob" name="dob" type="date" required>
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="i-country">Country that issued the document</label>
              <input id="i-country" name="country" type="text" required maxlength="60"
                     autocomplete="country-name" placeholder="United Kingdom">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="i-doc-type">Kind of document</label>
              <select id="i-doc-type" name="doc_type">
                <option value="passport">Passport</option>
                <option value="driving-licence">Driving licence</option>
                <option value="national-id">National identity card</option>
                <option value="residence-permit">Residence permit</option>
              </select>
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="i-doc">Photograph of the document</label>
              <input id="i-doc" name="doc" type="file" accept="image/*" capture="environment" required>
              <p class="muted xsmall">A flat, well-lit shot of the page carrying your photograph and your
              date of birth. JPEG, PNG, WebP or HEIC, under 6&nbsp;MB. You may cover the document number
              with your thumb — we do not need it.</p>
              <p class="id-preview" id="i-preview" aria-live="polite"></p>
            </div>
            <div class="declare">
              <input id="i-declare" name="declaration" type="checkbox" required>
              <label for="i-declare">I declare that this document is mine, that the name and date of birth
              above are true, and that I am eighteen or older. I understand a false declaration is recorded
              against this account and ends my use of the generators.</label>
            </div>
            <div class="ask-actions">
              <button class="btn" type="submit" id="i-send">Submit the check</button>
            </div>
          </form>
          <p class="auth-msg" id="i-msg" role="status"></p>

          <p class="muted xsmall">What we do with it: the photograph is stored privately in this project's
          own storage, is never published, never shown on the site, and is never given a public link. It is
          held so that a false declaration leaves evidence, and for no other purpose. The check is honest
          about what it is — a signed declaration with a document attached, not a forensic examination —
          and that is what stands behind every image and clip made here.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="auth-bio">
          <h3>Biometric entry</h3>
          <p class="muted small">Add a passkey and your device will let you back in with
          <strong>Face ID, Touch ID, Windows Hello, an Android fingerprint</strong> or a hardware key. The
          scan happens on your device and stays there: nothing biometric is sent here, ever. All this server
          keeps is a public key and the device's word — cryptographically signed — that it checked a real
          human.</p>
          <ul class="passkey-list" id="a-keys"></ul>
          <p class="ask-actions">
            <button class="btn" type="button" id="a-add-key">Enrol this device</button>
            <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="a-signout">Sign out</button>
          </p>
          <p class="auth-msg" id="a-bio-msg" role="status"></p>
          <p class="muted xsmall" id="a-bio-unsupported" hidden>This browser or device does not offer
          platform biometrics, so the emailed code remains your way in. Nothing is lost by that.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame reveal">
      <h3>What an account is for</h3>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li>The oracle greets you by name and keeps the thread of what you have asked &mdash; and so does ShakDrah on <a href="https://the-two-infinities.hatchable.site/">The Two Infinities</a>, because it is the same membership.</li>
        <li>Files you hand it stay attached to you rather than to a browser tab.</li>
        <li>Images and clips you make are gathered in one place instead of scattering.</li>
        <li>Nothing on this site is hidden behind it. There are no grades, no fees and no secrets withheld
        from the page — an account is a convenience, not an initiation.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="frame reveal">
      <h3>How the door is built</h3>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> <strong>No passwords.</strong> Nothing to reuse, leak, phish or reset.
        Proof of the address is a one-time code that expires in fifteen minutes.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> <strong>Passkeys, not fingerprints.</strong> WebAuthn keeps the
        biometric on your device's secure element; the server only ever sees a public key and a signature.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> <strong>User verification required.</strong> We reject any sign-in
        where the device did not actually check a face, a finger or a PIN.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> <strong>Sessions expire.</strong> Thirty days, revocable by signing
        out, and every passkey can be forgotten individually.</li>
        <li><span class="myth">◆</span> We will not sell the list, because there is nothing we want to sell
        it for.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
